{
  "title": "Making and Restoring Backups",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "30a6dc7500b8abd0",
      "text": "With wiki running in docker containers, the following commands are a means to backup the data."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "822345d5254f41fa",
      "text": "backing up one plot in the farm"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "53de0b3208956dc9",
      "text": "export DOMAIN=wiki.example.com\nexport TARBALL=\"backup.${DOMAIN}-$(date -I).tgz\"\ndocker-compose run -T farm \\\n  tar zcf - .wiki/${DOMAIN} \\\n  > $TARBALL"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7771cf00e8b8acdc",
      "text": "spot checking the contents of the backup"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "fd63b41fde656a20",
      "text": "tar ztf $TARBALL"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "89a175ebd78a9565",
      "text": "backing up the entire farm"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "669b5f23ee31789f",
      "text": "export TARBALL=\"backup-$(date -I).tgz\"\ndocker-compose run -T farm \\\n  tar zcf - .wiki \\\n  > $TARBALL"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "948073ecd16f6897",
      "text": "..."
    }
  ],
